WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.280
We often hear about genes only when&nbsp;
something goes wrong - when mutations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.240
mistakes made in the DNA sequence, cause&nbsp;
a disease like cancer or cystic fibrosis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.080
But what happens inside our cells that leads&nbsp;
from a mutation in DNA to the physical symptoms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.520
of a disease? Why do some mutations cause&nbsp;
positive outcomes, or no change at all?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.840
To answer these questions, we take a closer look&nbsp;
at how information flows from genes, to RNA,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.400
to proteins, to all the physical structures&nbsp;
and processes that make up living things.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.600
You might ask yourself what are the&nbsp;
relationships between genes and proteins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.920
this is such an important concept for biologists&nbsp;
that we've dabbed it the Central Dogma.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.160
The Central Dogma essentially&nbsp;
explains how biology works.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.560
The Central Dogma explains how the instruction&nbsp;
in DNA are converted into proteins and the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:03.680
this is done. First, the RNA polymerase reads the&nbsp;
code in the DNA and turns it into messenger RNA.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:11.200
mRNA is very similar in structure to DNA except&nbsp;
that it is single stranded. The mRNA then leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:17.440
the nucleus and goes out to the cytoplasm of the&nbsp;
cell. There it finds another set of proteins and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:23.440
it's a large protein complex made up of about 70&nbsp;
different proteins plus additional RNA molecules.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.960
This complex molecule is called the ribosome. The&nbsp;
ribosome decodes the message that's on the mRNA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.560
and converts it into a protein. So, the&nbsp;
Central Dogma explains this whole process from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:46.960
the stored code to a message to a protein,&nbsp;
and the proteins are who do all the work.

